@crew amadi-asha
// Asha Amadi (she/her), engine technician, days. The Works writer, batch 2. Sunny and dry; always by a window.
// Never admits climbing the garden's big tree. Never sings on purpose where people can hear.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Hey. New hand? Best window on Deck 5 is in the shuttle bay. Don't tell anyone.
- Oh, hello. Engines, days. If you need the overlook on Deck 6, it's past the coil rail.
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Morning. Lovely day. Well, it's always the same day out there. Still lovely.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance
- Hey, {me}. I was in the washroom earlier. You didn't hear anything. Good.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- {me}. Come here. Look out there. Nothing. Miles of nothing. Isn't it great?
? tier>=friend
- Oh, it's you. I saved you the window side. Friends get the best side.   #warm

== bye
- See you round.
- Bye! Find a window. Any window.

== feel
? mood:low
- Bit grey today. I'll find a window. That usually does it.
? mood:high
- Sunny side up today. Coils behaving, window seat free. What more is there?

== near
? act:work
- Coil two's lovely today. Look at the needle. Barely moving. Happy coil.
? act:dinner
- Late dinner, window seat, nobody in the queue. This is what winning looks like.   #funny

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- The whole washroom knows my songs. In order. I've stopped pretending they don't.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- The big tree in the garden? Never climbed it. Why, is there a leaf in my hair?   #funny

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- The best window aboard changes every week. This week it's the observatory.

// ---- Writer 2, batch 1: to ~30 (greet by time and warmth, near, invite, accept, decline, missed, birthday, cue)
== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:evening
- Evening. Late dinner for me. Mess is empty, window's free. Perfect.
? tier>=acquaintance warmth:cold
- Oh, there you are. I'd started checking windows for you. You weren't in any.   #funny

== near
? habit:music
- Music room in the evenings now. I just listen. Only listen. Honest.   #funny
? place:overlook
- Coils from the overlook. Best view on Deck 6. Well, the only view on Deck 6.   #funny

== invite
- Observatory tonight? I'll show you the window seat. It's the best one this week.
? tier>=colleague
- Friday jam? I won't sing. I'll sit. You can sit too. Sitting's nice.

== accept
- Ooh, yes. I'll bag us a window.
- Yes. Lovely. I'll be the one by the glass.

== decline
- Not tonight. Late dinner, window seat. It's booked. By me. Tomorrow?
? weekday:sat|sun
- Rest day. I'm doing a tour of every window on the ship. Another time?   #funny

== missed
- You missed it. That's all right. I had the window to myself. It was fine. Almost.

== birthday
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday! I'll give you the window side all day. That's a big present, that.   #warm
? birthday:me
- My birthday. The washroom sang to me this morning. All of them. Badly. I loved it.   #funny

== cue
? cue:repair.you@dept
- Was that your fix on Deck 6? The coils look happier. I'm telling everyone.

// ---- Writer 2, batch 1b: a hint (a moment is ready) and an about line for a named friend
== hint
- Got a minute later? I've saved a window. Not for the view, this time.

== about
? aff:salo-saad:friend
- Salo reads his twin's letters out at tea. I save him the window seat for it.

// ---- Writer 2, batch 6: bubbles (smalltalk, rumour), at most one in five about work. 60 characters.
== smalltalk
- Best window's in the shuttle bay.
- I wasn't singing. Nobody heard.   #funny
- Never climbed the tree. Never.   #funny
? time:evening
- Late dinner, window seat. Winning.   #funny
? act:work
- Coil two's happy. Look at it.
?

== rumour
- Bright side? Here's the bright side.
- Don't tell anyone. Except everyone.   #funny

// Writer 4, batch 11: goodbyes (leaving:you), packing (leaving:soon) and letters after they've moved on.
== feel
? leaving:soon
- Packing. Window seat on the shuttle's booked. Obviously.

== goodbye
? leaving:you tier>=acquaintance
- I'm off. Look on the bright side: someone else gets my window.
? leaving:you tier>=friend
- You found the good windows too. Best company for looking out of them. Thanks.   #warm

== letter
- New ship. Found the best window on day one. It's in the cargo bay. Of course it is.
? tier>=friend
- There's a tree in the new garden. Small one. I haven't climbed it. Yet. Hello from near a window.
